### ============================================================
### DevPulse / CSE 341 Team Project — REST Client test file
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
###
### HOW TO SWITCH BETWEEN LOCAL AND RENDER:
### Comment out one @baseUrl line and uncomment the other, then
### save the file — every request below uses {{baseUrl}}.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# @baseUrl = https://cse341-team-project-m1rm.onrender.com

### ============================================================
### AUTH
### Google OAuth can't be driven directly from a .rest file (it
### needs a real browser to complete the Google login screen), so:
###   1. Open {{baseUrl}}/login in your browser and log in with Google.
###   2. Open dev tools > Application/Storage > Cookies, copy the
###      value of the "connect.sid" cookie.
###   3. Paste it into @sessionCookie below.
### Every protected POST/PUT/DELETE request further down sends that
### cookie so it runs authenticated, just like your browser session.
### ============================================================

@sessionCookie = connect.sid=PASTE_YOUR_COOKIE_VALUE_HERE

### Check current login status (should flip to authenticated:true
### once @sessionCookie is set correctly)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/status

### Start the Google login flow (open this URL in a browser, not here)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/login

### Log out (clears the session on the server)
GET {{baseUrl}}/logout


### ============================================================
### USERS
### Joi schema: username (3-30, required), email (required),
### displayName (2-50, optional), bio (<=250, optional),
### avatarUrl (uri, optional)
### ============================================================

### Get all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Get a single user by ID (replace with a real _id from the GET above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE_USER_ID_HERE

### Create a user (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "username": "morgan_writes",
  "email": "morgan.writes@example.com",
  "displayName": "Morgan Lee",
  "bio": "Technical writer documenting APIs and dev tools.",
  "avatarUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1502685104226-ee32379fefbe"
}

### Create a user — missing required field (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "displayName": "No Username Or Email"
}

### Update a user (protected)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE_USER_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "username": "morgan_writes",
  "email": "morgan.writes@example.com",
  "displayName": "Morgan Lee-Fischer",
  "bio": "Technical writer and API documentation lead.",
  "avatarUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1502685104226-ee32379fefbe"
}

### Delete a user (protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/PASTE_USER_ID_HERE
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### Attempt to create a user WITHOUT auth (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "no_auth_user",
  "email": "no.auth@example.com"
}


### ============================================================
### CATEGORIES
### Joi schema: name (2-50, required), description (<=250, optional),
### slug (lowercase letters/numbers/hyphens only, required)
### ============================================================

### Get all categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories

### Get a single category by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/PASTE_CATEGORY_ID_HERE

### Create a category (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Testing",
  "description": "Unit testing, integration testing, and QA practices.",
  "slug": "testing"
}

### Create a category — invalid slug format (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Bad Slug Example",
  "description": "Slug has spaces and capitals, which should fail validation.",
  "slug": "Not A Valid Slug!"
}

### Update a category (protected)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/categories/PASTE_CATEGORY_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "name": "Testing & QA",
  "description": "Unit testing, integration testing, and quality assurance practices.",
  "slug": "testing-qa"
}

### Delete a category (protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/PASTE_CATEGORY_ID_HERE
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}


### ============================================================
### POSTS
### Joi schema: title (3-150, required), content (min 10, required),
### authorId (optional), categoryId (optional),
### tags (array of strings, optional), likesCount (int >=0, optional)
### ============================================================

### Get all posts
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts

### Get a single post by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/PASTE_POST_ID_HERE

### Create a post (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "title": "Writing Effective Integration Tests for Express APIs",
  "content": "Integration tests catch bugs that unit tests miss by exercising real routes, middleware, and error handling together.",
  "authorId": "PASTE_USER_ID_HERE",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID_HERE",
  "tags": ["testing", "express", "supertest"],
  "likesCount": 0
}

### Create a post — content too short (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "title": "Too Short",
  "content": "short"
}

### Update a post (protected)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/posts/PASTE_POST_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "title": "Writing Effective Integration Tests for Express APIs (Updated)",
  "content": "Integration tests catch bugs that unit tests miss by exercising real routes, middleware, and error handling together end to end.",
  "authorId": "PASTE_USER_ID_HERE",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID_HERE",
  "tags": ["testing", "express", "supertest", "jest"],
  "likesCount": 3
}

### Delete a post (protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/PASTE_POST_ID_HERE
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}


